    "repo": "swesmith/pandas-dev__pandas.95280573",
    "problem_statement": "IOHandles.close() clears created_handles before closing them\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using IOHandles context manager, if an error occurs during the closing of created handles, the handles list gets cleared before the actual closing happens, preventing proper cleanup.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport pandas.io.common as icom\nfrom io import BytesIO\n\nclass TestError:\n    def close(self):\n        raise OSError('test')\n\n# This should raise OSError but doesn't\nwith BytesIO() as buffer:\n    with icom.get_handle(buffer, 'rb') as handles:\n        handles.created_handles.append(TestError())\n```\n\nThe expected behavior is that the OSError from TestError.close() should be raised, but currently it's not because the created_handles list is cleared before attempting to close the handles."
  }
